# Rooted-Device Runbook (to hand a teammate)

Use ONLY when a real rooted device / emulator with ADB is available. Copy/paste-ready.

## 0. Device prerequisites
- USB debugging ON (Settings → Developer Options → USB debugging), OR a rooted emulator.
- `adb devices` shows the device as `device` (authorize the RSA prompt).
- Rooted device → magisk boot completed. Emulator → adb reachable.

## 1. Fast passive capture via adb (no Frida, no rebuild)
```bash
adb shell settings put global http_proxy 10.0.2.2:8888   # emulator host alias
adb shell settings put global http_proxy <PC-LAN-IP>:8888
# install the mitm CA as a USER cert:
adb push ~/.mitmproxy/mitmproxy-ca-cert.cer /sdcard/
# (no CLI for user certs — flow: Settings → Security → Install from storage)
# check traffic:
mitmweb --listen-port 8888 &
```

## 2. frida-server on the device
```bash
uname -a            # or: adb shell getprop ro.product.cpu.abi → arm64-v8a / x86_64
adb push frida-server-<version>-android-arm64 /data/local/tmp/frida-server
adb shell "chmod 755 /data/local/tmp/frida-server"
adb shell "/data/local/tmp/frida-server &" 
adb forward tcp:27042 tcp:27042
frida -U -f <package> --no-pause   # test connectivity
```
Laptop side: `pip install frida-tools` and use repo scripts (apkunpacker/FridaScripts,
abhirampatel/frida-android-scripts). Universal unpin + root-bypass + token-extract live there.

## 3. objection (automated, scripted calls, no custom JS required)
```bash
pip install --break-system-packages objection
objection -g <package> explore
# then inside the repl:
# android sslpinning disable
# android root disable
# android intent launch_activity com.target.Activity
# android heap search patterns --string "api_key|token|secret|Authorization"
# android keystore list
# android smtp get_class_methods com.target.MainActivity
exit
```

## 4. frida-dexdump for packed apps (android-runtime-frida skill §6)
```bash
pip install --break-system-packages frida-dexdump
frida-dexdump -U -f <package>            # dumps dexdump/ dir
jadx -d out <package>/*.dex              # real code of a packed target
```

## 5. drozer (component sweep — android-ipc-attack skill §6)
```bash
adb install drozer.apk
adb forward tcp:31415 tcp:31415
adb shell am start -n com.mwr.dz/.MainActivity; adb shell am broadcast -a com.mwr.dz.AIDL_INIT -e com.mwr.dz.transient true
drozer console connect
run app.package.attacksurface <pkg>
run scanner.provider.injection -a <pkg>
run scanner.provider.traversal -a <pkg>
```

## 6. Full rooted loop (deepest result, send artifacts back)
```
1. apkid <apk>                       → protectors to expect
2. frida-dexdump -U -f <pkg>          → real dex (if packed)
3. jadx -d dump/ <pkg>/*.dex
4. objection ... android sslpinning disable
5. adb shell settings put global http_proxy <PC>:8888
6. set phone to trust mitm CA
7. frida hooks: token_extract.js + key_capture.js (from android-runtime-frida skill)
8. drive UI / login / payment → capture API in mitmweb
9. ship HAR + dumped dex + hook output + screenshot evidence here
```

## 7. What the teammate should send back (always)
- `.har` of the session, or the PCAP/CSV
- `frida-dexdump` output dir (real DEX) if packed
- Hook stdout (`frida -U -f <pkg> -l token_extract.js > hook.log`)
- Screenshot of every PoC (evidence-hygiene skill rules: mask cookies/PII)
- Patched APK if they produced one

Format everything with the existing sweep deliverable layout so it lands in raw_findings.json cleanly.

